        'Present: Still played throughout Nigeria in families and youth centers',
      ],
      evolution: 'The game developed distinct rule variations: Normal Rules (allows duplicates in captures) and strict Yoruba Rules (forbids duplicates). Professional games use 3 rounds, amateur games use 4 rounds.',
      cultural: "Important part of Yoruba social life; used for teaching arithmetic and inductive logic to children. High-stakes gambling game for adults. Known locally as 'scooping' game.",
